# Line endings.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows and DEPLOYED to Linux. Without this,
# git checks shell scripts out with CRLF, and the server cannot even read the
# shebang: `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory`. Every script in
# deploy/ failed that way on the first real deploy, which is a confusing way to
# discover a line-ending setting.
#
# Anything executed by, or fed to, a Linux tool is pinned to LF.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile    text eol=lf
.dockerignore   text eol=lf
Caddyfile       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.example       text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.timer         text eol=lf

# Binary — never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
